    </content>
    <glossary>
    <definition id="def-00001"><term>401(k) plan</term><meaning>now the most common retirement plan in the United States, in which employers match employees’ contributions but leave them responsible for investing their own retirement account</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00002"><term>bridge employment</term><meaning>paid work after retirement, either in a similar job as before or in a new profession</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00003"><term>pension plan</term><meaning>the traditional retirement plan in the United States, in which employers provide a lifelong financial benefit to their retired employees</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00004"><term>phased retirement</term><meaning>the process of decreasing hours and responsibilities at work to retire gradually over a period of time</meaning></definition>
    </glossary>
</document>